WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.11 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
Reporting and communicating evidence

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Each audience needs its own report, honest from the very first one.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.170
Reporting shares your evidence with the people who need it, in a form each can use. Different audiences need different reports, but every one of them needs honesty.

4
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:26.170
Different audiences, different reports

5
00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:34.537
Co-founders and advisers: A short dashboard and the main risks. For example: One page each quarter: five indicators, traffic lights and two risks.

6
00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:42.163
Funders: Agreed formats and deadlines. For example: The six-month report a local grant asked for, in its own template.

7
00:00:42.163 --> 00:00:50.530
Customers and members: What their support or purchases achieved. For example: A cooperative’s yearly note: what members’ fees paid for and what changed.

8
00:00:50.530 --> 00:01:01.578
Participants and public: Accessible feedback and honest, simple stories backed by evidence. For example: A poster at the club in two languages: what we learned and changed.

9
00:01:01.978 --> 00:01:02.578
Why it matters

10
00:01:02.578 --> 00:01:08.252
1. A new initiative builds credibility when its claims match its data.

11
00:01:08.252 --> 00:01:13.185
2. Reporting what did not work shows that you learn.

12
00:01:13.185 --> 00:01:19.489
3. Reusing one set of data saves time for every audience.

13
00:01:19.889 --> 00:01:20.489
Where it goes next

14
00:01:20.489 --> 00:01:26.163
1. Your MEAL calendar: each report has a date and an owner.

15
00:01:26.163 --> 00:01:30.356
2. Your communications: evidence becomes messages and stories.

16
00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:37.030
3. The fuller reports funders, members or customers will ask for later.

17
00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.030
What to avoid

18
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.222
Presenting outputs as if they were outcomes.

19
00:01:42.222 --> 00:01:47.156
Claiming you caused a change you only contributed to.

20
00:01:47.156 --> 00:01:52.719
Recreating the data from scratch for every report.

21
00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:55.119
You build your reporting plan by audience.

22
00:01:55.119 --> 00:01:59.119
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

23
00:02:00.619 --> 00:02:03.719
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
